ss=\\"mq-root-block\\" mathquill-block-id=\\"1\\"><span mathquill-command-id=\\"3\\">3</span><var mathquill-command-id=\\"4\\">x</var><span mathquill-command-id=\\"5\\" class=\\"mq-binary-operator\\">−</span><span mathquill-command-id=\\"6\\">5</span></span></span>&nbsp;</span></span><br>","solution":""},{"type":"write","article":"<img alt=\\"\\" src=\\"/images/ee42b6ae6a4733f22db962c18c59c785.svg\\" style=\\"width: 550px; height: 611px;\\">​​​​​​​​​​​​​​<br><span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">The graph shows the momentum <em>y</em>, in newton-seconds, of an object <em>x</em> seconds after the object started moving, for<span class=\\"mq-math-mode\\" latex-data=\\"0\\\\le x\\\\le8\\"><span class=\\"mq-textarea\\"><textarea autocapitalize=\\"off\\" autocomplete=\\"off\\" autocorrect=\\"off\\" spellcheck=\\"false\\" x-palm-disable-ste-all=\\"true\\" data-cke-editable=\\"1\\" contenteditable=\\"false\\"></textarea></span><span class=\\"mq-root-block\\" mathquill-block-id=\\"1\\"><span mathquill-command-id=\\"3\\">&nbsp;0</span><span class=\\"mq-binary-operator\\" mathquill-command-id=\\"4\\">≤</span><var mathquill-command-id=\\"6\\">x</var><span class=\\"mq-binary-operator\\" mathquill-command-id=\\"7\\">≤</span><span mathquill-command-id=\\"9\\">8</span></span></span>. What is the average rate of change, in newton-seconds per second, in the momentum of the object from <span class=\\"mq-math-mode\\" latex-data=\\"x=2,x=6\\"><span class=\\"mq-textarea\\"><textarea autocapitalize=\\"off\\" autocomplete=\\"off\\" autocorrect=\\"off\\" spellcheck=\\"false\\" x-palm-disable-ste-all=\\"true\\" data-cke-editable=\\"1\\" contenteditable=\\"false\\"></textarea></span><span class=\\"mq-root-block\\" mathquill-block-id=\\"1\\"><var mathquill-command-id=\\"10\\">x</var><span class=\\"mq-binary-operator\\" mathquill-command-id=\\"11\\">=</span><span mathquill-command-id=\\"12\\">2 to&nbsp;</span><var mathquill-command-id=\\"17\\">x</var><span class=\\"mq-binary-operator\\" mathquill-command-id=\\"18\\">=</span><span mathquill-command-id=\\"19\\">6</span></span></span>&nbsp;?</span></span><br>","question":"","options":[],"correct":"1.25,5/4","solution":""},{"type":"choice","article":"​​​​​​​<span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\"><span class=\\"mq-math-mode\\" latex-data=\\"\\\\left(x+64\\\\right)^2=-100\\"><span class=\\"mq-textarea\\"><textarea autocapitalize=\\"off\\" autocomplete=\\"off\\" autocorrect=\\"off\\" spellcheck=\\"false\\" x-palm-disable-ste-all=\\"true\\" data-cke-editable=\\"1\\" contenteditable=\\"false\\"></textarea></span><span class=\\"mq-root-block\\" mathquill-block-id=\\"1\\"><span class=\\"mq-non-leaf\\" mathquill-command-id=\\"16\\"><span class=\\"mq-scaled mq-paren\\" style=\\"transform: scale(1, 1.2);\\">(</span><span class=\\"mq-non-leaf\\" mathquill-block-id=\\"17\\"><var mathquill-command-id=\\"6\\">x</var><span mathquill-command-id=\\"7\\" class=\\"mq-binary-operator\\">+</span><span mathquill-command-id=\\"8\\">6</span><span mathquill-command-id=\\"9\\">4</span></span><span class=\\"mq-scaled mq-paren\\" style=\\"transform: scale(1, 1.2);\\">)</span></span><span class=\\"mq-supsub mq-non-leaf mq-sup-only\\" mathquill-command-id=\\"12\\"><span class=\\"mq-sup\\" mathquill-block-id=\\"13\\"><span mathquill-command-id=\\"15\\">2</span></span></span><span class=\\"mq-binary-operator\\" mathquill-command-id=\\"18\\">=</span><span mathquill-command-id=\\"19\\" class=\\"\\">−</span><span mathquill-command-id=\\"20\\">1</span><span mathquill-command-id=\\"21\\">0</span><span mathquill-command-id=\\"22\\">0</span></span></span>&nbsp;</span></span><br><span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">How many distinct real solutions does the given equation have?</span></span><br>","question":"","options":[{"name":"A","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">Exactly one</span></span><br>"},{"name":"B","content":"Exactly two<br>"},{"name":"C","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">Infinitely many</span></span><br>"},{"name":"D","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">Zero</span></span><br>"}],"correct":"<span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">Zero</span></span><br>","solution":""},{"type":"choice","article":"<span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">|<span class=\\"mq-math-mode\\" latex-data=\\"x-8\\"><span class=\\"mq-textarea\\"><textarea autocapitalize=\\"off\\" autocomplete=\\"off\\" autocorrect=\\"off\\" spellcheck=\\"false\\" x-palm-disable-ste-all=\\"true\\" data-cke-editable=\\"1\\" contenteditable=\\"false\\"></textarea></span><span class=\\"mq-root-block\\" mathquill-block-id=\\"1\\"><var mathquill-command-id=\\"3\\">x</var><span mathquill-command-id=\\"4\\" class=\\"mq-binary-operator\\">−</span><span mathquill-command-id=\\"5\\">8</span></span></span>|&nbsp;<span class=\\"mq-math-mode\\" latex-data=\\"=11\\"><span class=\\"mq-textarea\\"><textarea autocapitalize=\\"off\\" autocomplete=\\"off\\" autocorrect=\\"off\\" spellcheck=\\"false\\" x-palm-disable-ste-all=\\"true\\" data-cke-editable=\\"1\\" contenteditable=\\"false\\"></textarea></span><span class=\\"mq-root-block\\" mathquill-block-id=\\"1\\"><span class=\\"mq-binary-operator\\" mathquill-command-id=\\"6\\">=</span><span mathquill-command-id=\\"7\\">1</span><span mathquill-command-id=\\"8\\">1</span></span></span>&nbsp;</span></span><br><span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">What is the sum of the solutions to the given equation?</span></span><br>","question":"","options":[{"name":"A","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">0</span></span><br>"},{"name":"B","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">16</span></span><br>"},{"name":"C","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">19</span></span><br>"},{"name":"D","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">22</span></span><br>"}],"correct":"<span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">16</span></span><br>","solution":""},{"type":"choice","article":"<span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">The manager of a gym selected a sample of 159 members at random to estimate the percentage of the gym's members that would continue to pay for a membership if the price increased. From the survey, the manager estimates that 88% of the gym's members would continue to pay for a membership if the price increased, with an associated margin of error of 5.05%. If the survey is repeated with a random sample of 318 members and the results are calculated in the same way, which of the following will be the most likely effect of using the larger random sample compared to the smaller random sample?</span></span><br>","question":"","options":[{"name":"A","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">The margin of error will be lower.</span></span><br>"},{"name":"B","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">The margin of error will be higher.</span></span><br>"},{"name":"C","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">The estimate of the percentage of the gym's members that would continue to pay for a membership if the price increased will be lower.</span></span><br>"},{"name":"D","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">The estimate of the percentage of the gym's members that would continue to pay for a membership if the price increased will be higher.</span></span><br>"}],"correct":"<span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">The margin of error will be lower.</span></span><br>","solution":""},{"type":"choice","article":"<span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">The maximum temperature on April 1. in degrees Fahrenheit (°F), was recorded each year at a certain weather station for 11 years. The histogram summarizes the recorded data set.</span></span><br><img alt=\\"\\" src=\\"/images/a3fe634e9b43fee812f807a8f67c3a00.svg\\" style=\\"width: 450px; height: 274px;\\">​​​​​​​​​​​​​​<br><span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">The temperature of <strong>76.2</strong> °<strong>F</strong> is removed from this data set to create a new data set of 10 temperatures. Which of the following statements must be true?<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">I.The mean of the new data set is less than the mean of the original data set.</span></span><br><span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">&nbsp; II.The median of the new data set is less than the median of the original data set.</span></span><br>","question":"","options":[{"name":"A","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">I only</span></span><br>"},{"name":"B","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">II only</span></span><br>"},{"name":"C","content":"<span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\"><span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\">I and II</span></span><br>"},{"name":"D","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">Neither I nor II</span></span><br>"}],"correct":"<span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">I only</span></span><br>","solution":""},{"type":"write","article":"<span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">For the positive quantities <em>h</em>,&nbsp;&nbsp;<em>j</em>, and <em>k</em>, 44% of <em>h</em> is equivalent to 62% of<em> j</em>, and <em>j</em> is equivalent to 22% of <em>k</em>. What percentage of <em>k </em>is <em>h</em>? (Disregard the % sign when entering your answer. For example, if your answer is 39%, enter 39)</span></span><br>","question":"","options":[],"correct":"31","solution":""},{"type":"choice","article":"<img alt=\\"\\" src=\\"/images/0f8f03fc06c9a729356882c6a4678fae.svg\\" style=\\"width: 500px; height: 457px;\\">​​​​​​​​​​​​​​<br><span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">The graph shows the relationship between the number of shares of stock from Company <em>A</em>,<em> x</em> , and the number of shares of stock from Company<em> B</em>, <em>y</em>, that Sayen can purchase. Which equation could represent this relationship?</span></span><br>","question":"","options":[{"name":"A","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:18px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\"><span class=\\"mq-math-mode\\" latex-data=\\"y=10x+18\\"><span class=\\"mq-textarea\\"><textarea autocapitalize=\\"off\\" autocomplete=\\"off\\" autocorrect=\\"off\\" spellcheck=\\"false\\" x-palm-disable-ste-all=\\"true\\" data-cke-editable=\\"1\\" contenteditable=\\"false\\"></textarea></span><span class=\\"mq-root-block\\" mathquill-block-id=\\"1\\"><var mathquill-command-id=\\"3\\">y</var><span class=\\"mq-binary-operator\\" mathquill-comman